[38;5;252m[1m## Four real divergences found and fixed in the Rust[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m1. All ten [38;5;10massert()[0ms were missing.[22m [38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m sets no [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m, so [38;5;10mCMAKE_C_FLAGS[0m is empty and [38;5;10mNDEBUG[0m is [3mnot[23m defined — confirmed by [38;5;10mU __assert_fail[0m in [38;5;10mnm -D[0m. The C therefore dies with [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m on inputs as ordinary as [38;5;10min_bytes == 0[0m, where the Rust returned a bogus [38;5;10m0[0m + error string. Added [38;5;10mcp_assert[0m, one per C assert, tagged with its [38;5;10mlib.c[0m line.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m2. [38;5;10mcp_dynamic[0m's stack-frame aliasing.[22m The repeat opcodes have no bound check on [38;5;10mn[0m, so [38;5;10mlens[288+32][0m overflows into the neighbouring locals. The original translation "fixed" this by padding the array. In the real C the stray bytes land on [38;5;10mlenlens[0m, [38;5;10msym[0m, [38;5;10mnlen[0m, [38;5;10mndst[0m, [38;5;10mnlit[0m, the three loop counters and finally [38;5;10mn[0m itself — and once [38;5;10mn[0m is overwritten it resets to 256 and the loop restarts, so [38;5;10mpinflate[0m never returns. The Rust returned normally instead. Rust now reproduces gcc's frame layout byte for byte (offsets read off [38;5;10mobjdump -d[0m), including gcc's ordering of [38;5;10mlens[n++] = sym[0m, where the increment is stored [3mbefore[23m the byte write. Also makes [38;5;10mlens[-1][0m correct: it aliases the top byte of the spilled state pointer, which is zero for any canonical x86-64 address.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m3 & 4. Two release-only miscompiles[22m, invisible in debug. [38;5;10mcp_decode[0m took [38;5;10ms: &mut cp_state_t[0m while [38;5;10mtree[0m points [3minto[23m that same state — [38;5;10m&mut[0m is [38;5;10mnoalias[0m to LLVM, and mixing it with raw pointers derived from it is also UB under Stacked Borrows. [38;5;10mcp_decode[0m's [38;5;10mtree[lo-1][0m read (reachable whenever [38;5;10mhi == 0[0m) then produced the wrong [38;5;10mkey[0m, so the Rust decoded garbage where the C aborted. Every internal function now takes [38;5;10m*mut cp_state_t[0m, no [38;5;10m&mut[0m is ever formed, and the tree pointers are derived from the struct base so the deliberate out-of-bounds read keeps valid provenance.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## What the C does that I replicated rather than fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mcp_ptr[0m mis-points for short stored blocks (the final-word refill inflates [38;5;10mcount[0m by more bits than it supplies), so a [38;5;10mLEN == 1[0m stored block copies the high byte of the [38;5;10mLEN[0m field, not the payload. [38;5;10mcp_build[0m returns [38;5;10mfirst[15][0m, which [3mexcludes[23m length-15 codes. [38;5;10mcp_stored[0m's [38;5;10mmemcpy[0m is bounded by neither buffer. Rows 1–6, 39 and 47 assert only C/Rust agreement for these.[0m[0m
